From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:41:31 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] platform-sgx

PC Engine SuperGrafx HuCards get their own shelf, Games/SGX, for .sgx
and .pce, on Beetle SuperGrafx alone (Platform::Sgx after Pico8,
Core::MednafenSupergrafx after Fake08). It plays and draws like the
TurboGrafx-16: B is II, A is I, START is Run, SELECT after the chord
hold, so Select and Run stay the soft reset; X and Y feed slot's turbo
for I and II; L1 and R1 stay slot's picture keys. The 2-button pad is
answered: no SuperGrafx card uses the 6-button one, whose III to VI
would need X, Y, L1 and R1.

The options are the TurboGrafx-16 list under the sgx_ prefix, plus
sgx_forcesgx enabled, so a .pce card the core's CRC table misses
(Darius Alpha) still gets the second VDC. The core declares no
frameskip option. The CD keys stay unanswered.

The Screen page gains a SuperGrafx section, last: Shader (the retro
list, Config/sgx_shader.txt) and Picture, which starts at Crop (8 lines
off the top and bottom) and walks Stretch, Actual and 4:3, kept in
Config/picture.txt as sgx. Saves are the 2 KB HUBM backup RAM in
Saves/SGX. The shelf release date is 8 December 1989. Until the cart
patch, a SuperGrafx card wears the TurboGrafx-16 HuCard.
